pkg:Evidence_v1_6_2 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.6.2 (PATCH release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "PATCH: processed the returned handover (HANDOVER_backlog-roadmap-framework_to_code-abundance-rdodi_v1_0_0.md, uploaded by the user) confirming BRSF adopted Proposal_BRSF_ProductScopeKind_v1_0_0.md in full at v1.143.0 (commit 42585ab). Pulled the framework update (TBox 1.62.0->1.63.0, SHACL 1.72.0 with the new ProductScopeKindShape, register 9.8.0->9.9.0), cross-checked the changelog entry against the handover document -- both agree. Applied hasProductScopeKind to all 3 Deliverables using the exact classification the original proposal specified: Del_AllStagesGateClean and Del_DisclosedLimitsPreserved as Kind_NonFunctional (verification/reliability and transparency claims respectively), Del_Stage4ConformsToCurrentDefault as Kind_Functional (the one actual capability). Re-verified against the new BRSF version: pipeline order unaffected (5/5 digests reproduce, ProductScopeKind touches no pipeline-tracked stage type), full SHACL 0 violations. Confirmed directly that the new ProductScopeKindShape advisory stays silent on this register (genuinely mixed 2/1 split), consistent with BRSF's own test-drive against its own mixed 1/1 case in the same release."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "6eeceb8e3050f851ce94963af99b65f1ba4b8937de093f61b82f6b437dd8487c"^^xsd:string .
